{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/TPS_SYST_01109","versions":[{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/TPS_SYST_01109@rel:R19-11#506d8eca","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/TPS_SYST_01109","release":"R19-11","content":"RTE fan-out support The RTE fan-out (signal fan-out) is de- scribed by the relation between SystemSignal and ISignal . In the case of a \"signal fan-out\", several ISignal s refer to the same SystemSignal as shown in the following example.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_TPS_SystemTemplate.pdf"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-01T10:12:27+00:00"},{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/TPS_SYST_01109@rel:R20-11#369c5390","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/TPS_SYST_01109","release":"R20-11","content":"RTE fan-out support for a SystemSignal The RTE fan-out (signal fan-out) from a SystemSignal to multiple ISignal s is enabled in the System Description if the following conditions apply: • several ISignal s reference the SystemSignal in the role systemSignal and • the SystemSignal is not referenced by a SystemSignalGroup • a DataMapping references the SystemSignal and • the DataMapping references an element in a PPortPrototype and • the ISignal s are transmitted by the EcuInstance on which the RTE is run- ning, i.e. an ISignalTriggering exists that references the ISignal in the role iSignal and references a ISignalPort of the EcuInstance with com- municationDirection out .","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_TPS_SystemTemplate.pdf"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-01T10:12:47+00:00"}],"lifecycle":{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/TPS_SYST_01109","is_dropped":true,"first_active_release":"R19-11","last_active_release":"R20-11","dropped_in":["R21-11","R22-11","R25-11"],"first_dropped_release":"R21-11","absent_before":["R18-10"],"platform_releases":["R18-10","R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R25-11"],"latest_platform_release":"R25-11"},"element":{"kind":"requirement","name":"","module":"SYST","cluster":"","pag